{"id":"conscience","name":"Conscience","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:conscience","torrey:conscience"],"groups":["Instances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Conscience","text":"That faculty of the mind, or inborn sense of right and wrong, by which we judge of the moral character of human conduct. It is common to all men. Like all our other faculties, it has been perverted by the Fall (John 16:2; Acts 26:9; Rom. 2:15). It is spoken of as “defiled” (Titus 1:15), and “seared” (1 Tim. 4:2). A “conscience void of offence” is to be sought and cultivated (Acts 24:16; Rom. 9:1; 2 Cor. 1:12; 1 Tim. 1:5, 19; 1 Pet. 3:21)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G4893","lemma":"συνείδησις","xlit":"syneídēsis","gloss":"co-perception","kjv":"conscience","count":26,"share":0.13},{"strong":"G2068","lemma":"ἐσθίω","xlit":"esthíō","gloss":"used only in certain tenses, the rest being supplied by","kjv":"devour, eat, live","count":9,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G266","lemma":"ἁμαρτία","xlit":"hamartía","gloss":"a sin","kjv":"offence, sin","count":10,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G2588","lemma":"καρδία","xlit":"kardía","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"heart","count":9,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G18","lemma":"ἀγαθός","xlit":"agathós","gloss":"\"good\"","kjv":"benefit, good, well","count":8,"share":0.04},{"strong":"G1438","lemma":"ἑαυτοῦ","xlit":"heautoû","gloss":"him- my-, thy-, our-, your-) self , etc.","kjv":"alone, her, himself, his","count":10,"share":0.05}],"verses":["John.8.9","Acts.23.1","Acts.24.16","Rom.2.15","Rom.9.1","Rom.13.5","1Cor.8.7","1Cor.8.10","1Cor.8.12","1Cor.10.28","1Cor.10.29","2Cor.1.12","2Cor.4.2","2Cor.5.11","1Tim.1.5","1Tim.1.19","1Tim.3.9","1Tim.4.2","Titus.1.15","Heb.9.14","Heb.10.2","Heb.10.22","Heb.13.18","1Pet.2.19","1Pet.3.16","1Pet.3.21","Gen.3.7","Gen.3.8","Gen.12.18","Gen.12.19","Gen.26.9","Gen.26.10","Gen.26.11","Gen.31.39","Gen.33.1","Gen.33.2","Gen.33.3","Gen.33.4","Gen.33.5","Gen.33.6","Gen.33.7","Gen.33.8","Gen.33.9","Gen.33.10","Gen.